## What to deliver

Build and rig the spire up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a fixed masonry base tower, a rail-arm set
into the mid-shaft, and a focus-ring crowning the top. This is a structure with no
caller controls: the interface is the two auto joints — **`rail_arm_slide`** that
rides the arm up and down, and **`focus_ring_spin`** that turns the ring a full
revolution — each driven by a looping auto-play animation **you author** as an
F-curve, while the base stays fixed. Produce **every** required part, joint, and
animation; you may add your own extra parts, joints, or auto-play animations on
top, but do not drop or contradict the required interface. When you are satisfied,
stop: the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished submission.
